{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794309056,"nonce":"ydumfmf5e1ZqazaPo3rO4m3DNSM=","title":"makeCloze should add the word when it has no status","message":"makeCloze (api/src/worker/user.ts) makes the card active = coalesce(word status = 'active', 1), so a cloze card can exist for a word with no status: active, but never served as new, since its lemma has no word cards and is never started (freshCards). The reader avoids it by calling setWord before makeCloze, two requests; the API doesn't. After unticking a word (clearWordStatus), its old cloze cards are inactive but a new one would be active. Fix: in makeCloze's transaction, when the word has no status, add it as setWord active does (word row, recognition and production cards); known/ignored keep the cloze inactive. Then the reader sends one request.","files":null}]}